<h2>Hybrid Insertion Sort</h2>
<p>
    Recursive algorithms that split the array into smaller sections, 
    such as 
    <a href="/algorithm?id=Quick">Quick Sort</a>
    or 
    <a href="/algorithm?id=Merge">Merge Sort</a>, 
    can be inefficient for small sections of the array,
    as the overhead of recursion outweighs the benefits of the algorithm.
    Hybrid Insertion Sort addresses this by switching to Insertion Sort for small sections,
    which is more efficient for small datasets.
    <br>
    <br>
    For algorithms such as these, 
    this visualization allows you to choose the maximum size of the section before 
    the algorithm switches to Insertion Sort.
    To update the maximum size before the algorithm switches to Insertion Sort,
    enter a number in the "Insertion Threshold" input box.
</p>